    "title": "Oceans Calling Festival Canceled Due to Massive Nor'Easter Storm - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff ,\n1 days ago The impeding inclement weather made it impossible for the festival to take place. The 2026 Oceans Calling Festival has been completely canceled after a strengthening nor’easter brought dangerous coastal conditions to Ocean City, Maryland, wiping out one of the biggest music weekends of the year on the East Coast. The three-day festival was scheduled to take place September 25-27 along the Ocean City Boardwalk and Inlet Beach, with Dave Matthews Band, Twenty One Pilots and Mumford & Sons serving as the three main headliners. Organizers initially hoped they could salvage most of the weekend after canceling only Friday’s opening day, but deteriorating forecasts, flooding, elevated tides and powerful winds ultimately made it impossible to safely continue building and operating the sprawling beachfront festival site. On Friday, September 25, organizers announced that the entire 2026 event had been called off. Read full article",
